Update crates flagged by RustSec to their newest semver-compatible
releases with `cargo update -p <crate>@<version> --precise <version>`:
  actix-files 0.7.0 -> 0.7.4 (RUSTSEC-2026-0443)
  actix-http 3.13.3 -> 3.21.0 (RUSTSEC-2026-0446, -0448, -0455)
  actix-web 4.15.0 -> 4.19.0 (RUSTSEC-2026-0447)
  crossbeam-epoch 0.9.18 -> 0.9.21 (RUSTSEC-2026-0204)
  h2 0.4.14 -> 0.4.19 (RUSTSEC-2026-0258)
  pulldown-cmark 0.13.4 -> 0.13.6 (RUSTSEC-2026-0414, -0433)
  rand 0.8.5 -> 0.8.8 (RUSTSEC-2026-0097)
  rustix 1.1.5 -> 1.1.6 (RUSTSEC-2026-0486)
  rustls 0.23.45 -> 0.23.46 (RUSTSEC-2026-0346 to -0349)
  tokio 1.53.1 -> 1.54.1 (RUSTSEC-2026-0386)
  zstd 0.13.3 -> 0.13.5 (RUSTSEC-2026-0391)
  zstd-safe 7.2.4 -> 7.4.1 (RUSTSEC-2026-0395 to -0406)
  zstd-sys 2.0.16 -> 2.1.3 (RUSTSEC-2026-0410)
The newer actix crates also take actix-web-codegen 4.5.0, http-range
0.1.6, brotli 9.1.1 with brotli-decompressor 6.3.1, alloc-no-stdlib 3.0.0
and alloc-stdlib 0.3.0, and add zstd 0.14.4 and zstd-safe 8.3.0 beside
the 0.13/7.x pair. The windows-sys and similar re-selections cargo made
alongside are left out.

Not covered, as no semver-compatible release fixes them: crypto-bigint
0.5 (RUSTSEC-2026-0387), h2 0.3 (RUSTSEC-2026-0258), rsa 0.9
(RUSTSEC-2023-0071) and ruzstd 0.8 (RUSTSEC-2026-0344). The other flagged
crates in the lockfile are not in the qdrant binary's build.

